class:: ShaderWaveformTexture
summary:: Controlled-rate recent-waveform stream for SCShader's spectrum binding
categories:: External>Graphics
related:: Guides/SCShader, Classes/ShaderBuffer, Classes/ShaderFFTTexture, Classes/Shader

description::
ShaderWaveformTexture samples a recent window from a mono audio bus and writes its values into an owned link::Classes/ShaderBuffer::. At each requested visual update, a bank of delay-and-latch readers captures points across the recent code::window:: duration. The resulting one-row Float32 GPU texture shares the fixed code::spectrum:: binding with link::Classes/ShaderFFTTexture::, so bind it with code::shader.setTexture(\spectrum, waveform)::.

This is a visual-rate snapshot, not an audio-rate oscilloscope and not a replacement for a SuperCollider Scope. It favors a bounded, explicit 2 through 8192 point count and blob transfer into the renderer over unbounded server polling. Relative to vanilla code::DelayN:: and code::Latch::, it combines those familiar UGens into a renderer-mappable waveform resource.

classmethods::

method:: new

argument:: server
Booted audio Server that owns code::source::.

argument:: source
Non-negative mono audio-bus index.

argument:: points
Number of captured samples from 2 through 8192. Defaults to 512.

argument:: window
Recent capture duration in seconds. Must be positive. Defaults to 0.05.

argument:: rate
Positive reply rate in Hz. Defaults to 30.

argument:: shaderServer
Ready ShaderServer that owns the resulting ShaderBuffer. Defaults to code::ShaderServer.default::.

instancemethods::

method:: start

discussion::
Creates the capture Synth and OSC responder. Call it from a Routine because it synchronizes the generated SynthDef. The capture Synth runs at the audio server's default-group tail.

method:: free

discussion::
Frees the OSC responder, capture Synth, and owned ShaderBuffer.

